# Weekly Mini Project 04 — Blood Donation Network

## 1. Purpose

This document explains how the **Blood Donation Network** project is organized.

The project is an emergency blood donation coordination platform built with **React + TypeScript** (using React Context for state) on the frontend, **NestJS + TypeScript** (with DTO validation, JWT authentication, role guards, Swagger, and custom domain logging) on the backend, and **PostgreSQL** accessed through **Prisma ORM** for persistent relational storage.

The backend decides every important business rule: blood-type red-cell compatibility (R-1, R-2), the 56-day post-donation rest period (R-3..R-5), donor eligibility and ranked matching (R-6..R-8), request lifecycle transitions (R-9..R-14), active pledge limits and automatic release (R-15..R-18), atomic donation recording inside a database transaction (R-19..R-22), and role/privacy enforcement (R-23, R-24). The frontend only displays what the backend returns and guides the user.

**Every name, route, method signature, DTO property order, TypeScript interface, CSS variable, and file owner in this document is fixed.** Need a new shared name or a contract change? Ask the team lead (Eyad Ibrahim) first.

