## 3. Technology

### Frontend

- React, TypeScript, Vite, React Router (`react-router-dom`)
- **React Context** for state (one context per feature: `AuthContext`, `DonorContext`, `RequestsContext`)
- Hooks: `useState`, `useEffect`, `useCallback`, `useMemo`, `useContext`
- Plain CSS, one file per page or component, using CSS variables from `client/src/styles/theme.css` and strict BEM owner prefixes
- API service layer in `client/src/services/` (`http.ts`, `auth.api.ts`, `donors.api.ts`, `pledges.api.ts`, `requests.api.ts`)
- `localStorage` only for persisting the JWT token (`bdn.token`) managed exclusively by `AuthContext` / `http.ts`

### Backend

- Node.js, NestJS, TypeScript
- **PostgreSQL** database accessed through **Prisma ORM** (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts`)
- Architecture: **Controller → Service → Persistence (Prisma)**. Controllers contain zero business rules and zero database queries
- **JWT authentication** (`@nestjs/jwt`, `bcrypt`) with backend guards (`JwtAuthGuard`, `RolesGuard`) enforcing `COORDINATOR` and `DONOR` roles while keeping public endpoints (`@Public()`) deliberately open and returning public fields only
- **DTO classes** with `class-validator` and `class-transformer`
- One global `ValidationPipe` (`common/validation.pipe.ts` with `whitelist: true`, `forbidNonWhitelisted: true`, `stopAtFirstError: true`)
- One global `AllExceptionsFilter` (`common/all-exceptions.filter.ts`) returning `{ "message": "..." }`
- **Swagger / OpenAPI** (`@nestjs/swagger`) at `/api/docs` documenting every endpoint, summary, resource tag, body, parameter, and Bearer auth requirement
- **Custom Logger** (`common/app-logger.service.ts`) recording meaningful domain events (request created, cancelled, fulfilled; donation recorded; rejected donation attempts with reason—never logging every HTTP request and never logging passwords or tokens)

### Not allowed (Out of Scope)

- Redux, Zustand, React Query, or any external state management library
- Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, Material UI, or any external UI/CSS component library
- Maps or external location/geocoding services
- SMS, email, or push notification services
- Payments or billing systems
- Real hospital/blood-bank ERP, laboratory/blood-testing systems, blood-unit inventory/storage/expiry tracking, or medical fitness diagnosis
- WebSockets, GraphQL, mobile apps, Docker, or cloud deployment

