## 6. Pages

### SOS Board (`/`) — Owner: Molham

Uses `useRequests()` (`sosRequests`, `isSosLoading`, `sosError`, `loadSosRequests`) and `useAuth()`.

- Displays a crimson hero banner explaining the platform's mission ("When a patient needs blood urgently, find the right donors in the right area — fast") with call-to-action buttons (**Become a Donor** / **Sign In**, or **Go to Dashboard** if signed in).
- Displays all `OPEN` requests ordered by urgency (`CRITICAL` → `HIGH` → `NORMAL`) and then by creation time (`oldest first`), exactly as returned by `GET /api/requests/sos`.
- Each `SosRequestCard` shows **only public data** (FR-8, R-23): `BloodTypeBadge`, `UrgencyBadge`, area name, hospital name, `unitsStillNeeded` ("X units still needed"), and relative/formatted creation time. Never shows patient references, notes, or donor personal data.
- Includes `Loading`, `ErrorMessage` (with retry), and `EmptyState` ("No active SOS blood requests right now. All current hospital needs have been met.") when there are zero open requests (Section 13: "Empty state, not an error").

### Sign In (`/sign-in`) & Donor Sign Up (`/sign-up`) — Owner: Molham

Uses `useAuth()`.

- **Sign In (`/sign-in`)**: Form with `identifier` (phone number or email) and `password`. Supports signing in as either a `COORDINATOR` or a `DONOR` (FR-2). Shows `authError` inline next to the form (never only in console). On success, redirects `COORDINATOR` to `/coordinator/requests` and `DONOR` to `/donor/dashboard`.
- **Donor Sign Up (`/sign-up`)**: Calls `loadAreas()` on mount. Form with `fullName`, `phone`, optional `email`, `password`, `bloodType` selector (all 8 blood types), and `areaId` selector (populated from `GET /api/areas`) (FR-1). Shows validation and conflict errors (`400` / `409`) inline inside the form. On success, signs the donor in and redirects to `/donor/dashboard`.

### Donor Dashboard (`/donor/dashboard`) — Owner: Taymaa

Uses `useDonor()` (`profile`, `eligibleRequests`, `loadMyProfile`, `loadEligibleRequests`, `createPledge`, `withdrawPledge`).

- **Eligibility Status Banner (`EligibilityBanner`)**: Displays the donor's calculated `eligibilityStatus` from the backend (FR-4):
  - `ELIGIBLE`: Green status banner — `"Eligible to donate now"`.
  - `REST_PERIOD`: Amber status banner — `"In rest period until [formatted nextAllowedDonationDate]"` and explains the 56-day post-donation cooldown.
  - `UNAVAILABLE`: Neutral/muted banner — `"Currently marked as unavailable"` with a quick link to `/donor/profile` to turn availability back on.
  - `INACTIVE`: Red banner — `"Account is deactivated"`.
- **Active Pledge Card (`ActivePledgeCard`)**: Shows the donor's current `PLEDGED` pledge (at most one across all requests, R-16) with blood type, hospital, area, urgency badge, and a **Withdraw pledge** button (`PATCH /api/pledges/:id/withdraw`). When clicked, updates the active pledge card and eligible requests list immediately without reload.
- **Requests I Can Help With (`EligibleRequestsList`)**: Displays `GET /api/donors/me/eligible-requests` (FR-10) ordered like the SOS board (`CRITICAL` first, then oldest first). Each item has a **Pledge to donate** button (`POST /api/requests/:id/pledges`). Any business-rule rejection (e.g., already holding an active pledge, rest period, or active pledges reached `unitsStillNeeded`) is shown clearly inline (`actionError`). Has loading, error, and empty states.
- **Donation History (`DonationHistoryTable`)**: Lists the donor's past recorded donations (date, hospital, area, blood type, 1 unit) (FR-4), with an empty state if the donor has not donated yet.

### Donor Profile (`/donor/profile`) — Owner: Taymaa

Uses `useDonor()` and `useAuth()` (for `areas` and `signOut`).

- Displays read-only identity fields (`fullName`, `bloodType`, `email`, `lastDonationDate`, `nextAllowedDonationDate`).
- **Edit Profile Form**: Allows the donor to update their `areaId`, `phone`, and `isAvailable` toggle (`Available` / `Unavailable`) via `PATCH /api/donors/me` (FR-3, R-24). Shows a success confirmation banner and inline backend validation/conflict errors.
- **Deactivate Account Section**: Danger zone with a confirmation step calling `PATCH /api/donors/me/deactivate` (FR-3). Deactivating sets `isActive = false`, automatically withdraws any active pledge, and signs the user out (or updates state).

### Coordinator Requests (`/coordinator/requests`) — Owner: Rami

Uses `useRequests()` (`requests`, `loadRequests`, `createRequest`) and `useAuth()` (`areas`, `loadAreas`).

- **Filter Bar (`RequestFiltersBar`)**: Filter controls for `status` (`All`, `OPEN`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED`), `bloodType` (`All` or any of the 8 types), `areaId` (`All` or any area), and `urgency` (`All`, `CRITICAL`, `HIGH`, `NORMAL`) (FR-7). Changing filters updates URL query parameters and calls `loadRequests(filters)`.
- **Create SOS Request Modal/Form (`CreateRequestModal`)**: Allows the coordinator to publish a new SOS request with `patientReference` (internal code, not a patient name), `bloodType`, `unitsRequired` (integer `1`–`10`), `areaId`, `urgency`, `hospital`, and optional `note` (FR-5). Displays backend `400` or `409` (duplicate open request with same `patientReference` and `bloodType`, R-13) errors clearly next to the form.
- **Requests Table / Grid**: Shows each request's patient reference, blood type badge, urgency badge, status badge (`OPEN`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED`), area, hospital, progress (`unitsCollected / unitsRequired` and `unitsStillNeeded`), creation time, and links to **Request Details** (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId`) and **Eligible Donors** (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId/eligible-donors`).

### Request Details (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId`) — Owner: Rami

Uses `useRequests()` (`currentRequest`, `loadRequestById`, `updateRequest`, `cancelRequest`, `recordDonation`).

- Shows all request data: `patientReference`, `bloodType`, `urgency`, `status`, `area`, `hospital`, `note`, `cancelReason` (if cancelled), `createdAt`, and unit counters: **Units Required**, **Units Collected**, and **Units Still Needed** (FR-13).
- Link button to **Find Eligible Donors** (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId/eligible-donors`) when `status === 'OPEN'`.
- **Coordinator Actions (only enabled when `status === 'OPEN'`, R-9, R-14)**:
  - **Update Request (`UpdateRequestForm`)**: Edit `unitsRequired` (cannot be less than `unitsCollected`, R-12), `urgency`, and `note` (`PATCH /api/requests/:id`).
  - **Cancel Request (`CancelRequestModal`)**: Cancel with a required `cancelReason` (`PATCH /api/requests/:id/cancel`, Flow E).
  - **Record Donation (`RecordDonationModal`)**: Record a completed donation for a donor (`donorId` and `donationDate`, defaulting to today, `POST /api/requests/:id/donations`, Flow D).
- **Pledges List**: Shows all pledges for this request (donor full name, blood type, phone, status badge `PLEDGED` / `COMPLETED` / `WITHDRAWN` / `RELEASED`, pledge time) and a quick **Record Donation** button next to any `PLEDGED` donor.
- **Recorded Donations List**: Shows all completed donations on this request (donor name, blood type, donation date, 1 unit, recorded by coordinator).
- All backend rejections (`400` / `409`, such as trying to record a donation for a donor in rest period with exact date) are displayed prominently on screen. After any action, counters, status, pledges, and donations update immediately without a page reload.

### Eligible Donors (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId/eligible-donors`) — Owner: Rami

Uses `useRequests()` (`currentRequest`, `eligibleDonorsResult`, `loadRequestById`, `loadEligibleDonors`, `recordDonation`).

- Displays a summary header of the target request (patient reference, needed blood type, area, urgency, units still needed) and a link back to `/coordinator/requests/:requestId`.
- **Excluded Donors Summary (`ExcludedDonorsSummary`)**: Displays the backend's `excludedSummary` counts of compatible donors in the same area who were excluded, grouped by reason (FR-9, R-8):
  - **In Rest Period (`restPeriod`)**: count of compatible donors in the area currently inside their 56-day cooldown.
  - **Unavailable (`unavailable`)**: count of active, non-resting compatible donors in the area who set `isAvailable = false`.
  - **Inactive (`inactive`)**: count of compatible donor accounts in the area with `isActive = false`.
- **Ranked Eligible Donors List (`EligibleDonorRow`)**: Displays the ranked list returned by `GET /api/requests/:id/eligible-donors` (FR-9, R-7: exact blood-type match first, then other compatible types; within each group, longest time since last donation or never donated first; then alphabetical by name). Each row shows rank number, donor full name, phone, `BloodTypeBadge`, an **Exact Match** vs **Compatible** tag, area name, `lastDonationDate` (or `"Never donated"`), whether they have an active pledge on this request, and a **Record Donation** button that opens the record-donation confirmation right away.

### Not Found (`*`) — Owner: Molham

A friendly 404 page with a link back to the Public SOS Board (`/`).

