### 8.3 Central Matching & Eligibility Engine (`api/src/matching/` — Owner: Eyad Ibrahim)

`MatchingService` centralizes all blood compatibility, rest-period, and donor-ranking rules so neither `RequestsService`, `DonationsService`, `DonorsService`, nor `PledgesService` ever duplicates rule logic:

| Method | Responsibility & Rules Enforced |
| --- | --- |
| `isBloodCompatible(neededType, donorType)` | Returns `true` if `donorType` is in `BLOOD_COMPATIBILITY_MAP[neededType]` (R-1, R-2) |
| `getCompatibleDonorTypes(neededType)` | Returns the compatible donor blood types for `neededType` (R-1) |
| `getNextAllowedDonationDate(lastDonationDate)` | Returns `null` if `lastDonationDate` is `null` (R-5); otherwise returns `lastDonationDate + REST_PERIOD_DAYS (56 days)` as `YYYY-MM-DD` (R-3, R-4) |
| `isInRestPeriod(lastDonationDate, now)` | Returns `true` when `lastDonationDate` exists and `today < nextAllowedDonationDate` (R-4, R-5) |
| `getDonorEligibilityStatus(donor, now)` | Returns `'INACTIVE'` if `!donor.user.isActive`, `'REST_PERIOD'` if in rest period, `'UNAVAILABLE'` if `!donor.isAvailable`, otherwise `'ELIGIBLE'` (FR-4) |
| `checkDonorEligibilityForRequest(donor, request, now)` | Checks R-6 in exact order: (1) account active, (2) donor available, (3) not in rest period (returning `nextAllowedDonationDate` in message), (4) blood type compatible, (5) area matches request area. Returns `{ eligible: boolean; reason?: string; code?: 'INACTIVE' \| 'UNAVAILABLE' \| 'REST_PERIOD' \| 'INCOMPATIBLE_BLOOD' \| 'DIFFERENT_AREA' }` |
| `getEligibleDonorsForRequest(requestId)` | Evaluates all donors in the request's area with compatible blood types. Separates excluded donors into `{ restPeriod, unavailable, inactive }` counts (R-8) and orders eligible donors by: (1) exact blood-type match (`donor.bloodType === request.bloodType`) before other compatible types, (2) oldest `lastDonationDate` first (`null` / never donated comes first), (3) `fullName` ascending (`localeCompare`) (R-7) |

