## 9. Where Each Business Rule Is Enforced

Every business rule is enforced by the backend. The frontend only guides the user and displays backend state and error messages.

| Rule ID | Rule Summary | Backend (Enforces & Decides) | Frontend (Guides & Displays) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **R-1, R-2** | Red-cell blood-type compatibility table | `MatchingService.isBloodCompatible` & `BLOOD_COMPATIBILITY_MAP` in `common/constants.ts` | Never computes compatibility; displays `BloodTypeBadge` and backend lists |
| **R-3** | Single configured rest period (`56` days) | `REST_PERIOD_DAYS = 56` in `common/constants.ts` | Displays rest period explanation and backend dates |
| **R-4, R-5** | `nextAllowedDonationDate = lastDonationDate + 56 days`; `null` if never donated | `MatchingService.getNextAllowedDonationDate` & `isInRestPeriod` | Shown on `EligibilityBanner`, `DonorProfilePage`, and rejection alerts |
| **R-6** | Donor eligible only when active, available, not in rest period, compatible blood type, and same area | `MatchingService.checkDonorEligibilityForRequest` | Shows only eligible requests on Donor Dashboard and eligible donors on Coordinator screen |
| **R-7** | Eligible-donor ranking: exact blood match first, then compatible; oldest `lastDonationDate` (or never donated) first; then by `fullName` | `MatchingService.getEligibleDonorsForRequest` | Renders rows in the exact order returned by the API |
| **R-8** | Excluded-donor summary counts compatible donors in same area grouped by `restPeriod`, `unavailable`, `inactive` without exposing personal data to public | `MatchingService.getEligibleDonorsForRequest` | `ExcludedDonorsSummary` cards on `EligibleDonorsPage` |
| **R-9, R-14** | Request is `OPEN`, `FULFILLED`, or `CANCELLED`; only `OPEN` requests can be updated, cancelled, pledged to, matched, or receive donations; `FULFILLED`/`CANCELLED` cannot be reopened | `RequestsService`, `PledgesService`, `DonationsService` throw `409 Conflict` | Update, Cancel, Record Donation, and Pledge buttons only shown when `status === 'OPEN'` |
| **R-10** | `unitsStillNeeded = unitsRequired - unitsCollected` (never negative) | Calculated in `RequestsService` & `DonorsService` response mappers | Displays `unitsRequired`, `unitsCollected`, `unitsStillNeeded` from API |
| **R-11** | When `unitsCollected` reaches `unitsRequired`, request becomes `FULFILLED` automatically | `DonationsService.recordDonation` & `RequestsService.updateRequest` | Status badge automatically updates to `FULFILLED` |
| **R-12** | `unitsRequired` cannot be reduced below `unitsCollected` | `RequestsService.updateRequest` throws `400 Bad Request` | Form input sets `min={request.unitsCollected}` and displays backend error |
| **R-13** | Two `OPEN` requests with same `patientReference` and same `bloodType` are not allowed | `RequestsService.createRequest` throws `409 Conflict` | Shows conflict message inside `CreateRequestModal` |
| **R-15** | Donor can pledge only to an `OPEN` request they are eligible for | `PledgesService.createPledge` checks `OPEN` (409) and `MatchingService.checkDonorEligibilityForRequest` (400 with exact reason) | Displays backend reason (including `nextAllowedDonationDate` if in rest period) |
| **R-16** | Donor can hold at most one active (`PLEDGED`) pledge at a time across all requests | `PledgesService.createPledge` checks existing `PLEDGED` pledge (409) | Disables pledge buttons or shows backend conflict message when holding an active pledge |
| **R-17** | Request cannot have more active (`PLEDGED`) pledges than `unitsStillNeeded` | `PledgesService.createPledge` checks `activePledgesCount >= unitsStillNeeded` (409) | Displays backend conflict message |
| **R-18** | When request becomes `FULFILLED` or `CANCELLED`, remaining `PLEDGED` pledges become `RELEASED` | `DonationsService.recordDonation`, `RequestsService.updateRequest`, `RequestsService.cancelRequest` inside `prisma.$transaction` | Pledge badges update to `RELEASED` |
| **R-19, R-20** | Donation recorded only for `OPEN` request and currently eligible donor; counts as `1` unit | `DonationsService.recordDonation` verifies `OPEN` (409) and `MatchingService` eligibility (400) | Displays error message; nothing changes on failure |
| **R-21** | `donationDate` cannot be in the future | `DonationsService.recordDonation` checks `donationDate <= ClockService.now()` (400) | Date picker sets `max={today}` and shows backend error |
| **R-22** | Recording donation, incrementing `unitsCollected`, completing donor's pledge, updating `lastDonationDate`, and fulfilling request + releasing other pledges happen in **one database transaction** | `prisma.$transaction` in `DonationsService.recordDonation` | Reloads request details and eligible donors after transaction completes |
| **R-23** | Public endpoints and SOS board never return donor names, phone numbers, patient references, or notes | `RequestsService.getPublicSosRequests` selects and returns only public fields | `SosBoardPage` renders only public fields |
| **R-24** | A donor can read and change only their own profile, pledges, and history | `DonorsController` & `PledgesController` extract `user.id` from JWT `@CurrentUser()` | Donor screens use `/donors/me` and own pledge IDs |

## 10. What the Backend Calculates

Only the backend calculates or decides:

```text
blood-type compatibility (R-1, R-2)
nextAllowedDonationDate and whether a donor is in rest period (R-3..R-5)
donor eligibility status: ELIGIBLE | REST_PERIOD | UNAVAILABLE | INACTIVE
whether a donor is eligible for a specific request and the exact rejection reason (R-6)
ranked order of eligible donors and excluded-donor counts by reason (R-7, R-8)
unitsStillNeeded = Math.max(0, unitsRequired - unitsCollected) (R-10)
automatic transition to FULFILLED and pledge release to RELEASED (R-11, R-18)
```

The frontend must **never**:

- hardcode or evaluate the blood-type compatibility table
- add 56 days to `lastDonationDate` to decide if a donor is in rest period
- filter or rank eligible donors on the client
- calculate `unitsStillNeeded` on its own

The only constants in `client/src/constants.ts` are display lists (`BLOOD_TYPES`, `URGENCY_LEVELS`, `REQUEST_STATUSES`) and input bounds (`MIN_UNITS = 1`, `MAX_UNITS = 10`) used strictly to render dropdowns and HTML form attributes.

