### How `http.ts` works

- Reads the JWT token from `localStorage` under the key `bdn.token` (wrapped in `try/catch`).
- If a token exists, automatically attaches `Authorization: Bearer <token>` to the request headers.
- Parses JSON responses and throws `new ApiError(response.status, body.message)` when `!response.ok`.
- Turns network failures (`fetch` rejection) into `new ApiError(0, 'Cannot reach the server. Please check your connection and try again.')`.

