## 14. CSS Rules & BEM Prefixes

Plain CSS is global, so class names must never clash across team members.

1. Colors come only from `theme.css`.
2. Every class starts with its owner prefix using strict BEM notation (`prefix__element--modifier`).
3. No bare element selectors (`button`, `input`, `table`, `h1`, `a`) outside `global.css`.
4. A page's CSS file is imported only by that page.
5. Never style or override another owner's classes.

