## 15. Naming Conventions

### Data

- JSON fields: `camelCase`.
- Dates (donation date, next allowed donation date, last donation date): `YYYY-MM-DD` (example: `2026-12-12`).
- Timestamps (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`): ISO 8601 string (`2026-11-01T09:10:00.000Z`).
- Blood types in API & frontend: `'O-' | 'O+' | 'A-' | 'A+' | 'B-' | 'B+' | 'AB-' | 'AB+'`.
- Enums in API & frontend: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (`COORDINATOR`, `DONOR`, `CRITICAL`, `HIGH`, `NORMAL`, `OPEN`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED`, `PLEDGED`, `COMPLETED`, `WITHDRAWN`, `RELEASED`, `ELIGIBLE`, `REST_PERIOD`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `INACTIVE`).

### Backend

- Files: `<name>.controller.ts`, `<name>.service.ts`, `<name>.module.ts`, `<name>.guard.ts`, `<name>.decorator.ts`, `<name>.util.ts`, `<name>.types.ts`, and `<name>.dto.ts` inside `dto/`.
- Classes: `PascalCase` (DTOs end with `Dto`). Methods and variables: `camelCase`. Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- Always use `ClockService.now()` for current time checks in services. Never call `new Date()` directly for business-rule comparisons.

### Frontend

- Components and pages: `PascalCase`. Each page has `<Name>Page.tsx` and `<Name>Page.css`.
- Contexts: `<Feature>Context.tsx`, exporting `<Feature>Provider` and `use<Feature>()`.
- Hooks start with `use`. Event handlers start with `handle`. Booleans start with `is`, `has`, or `can`.
- Shared utilities (Owner: **Molham**):

| File | Functions | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `utils/format.ts` | `formatDate(dateStr)`, `formatDateTime(isoStr)`, `formatUnits(units)`, `formatPhone(phone)` | Molham |
| `utils/date.ts` | `toDateString(date)`, `getTodayString()` | Molham |

### Git

- Branches: `be/<module>-<description>` or `fe/<page>-<description>`.
- Commits: `type(scope): message` (`feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `chore`).

